---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../config/site';

const { legal, email, formEndpoint, analyticsId } = SITE;
const entity = legal.entityName || SITE.name;
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How All Set Consulting collects, uses and protects personal information, under the EU GDPR and the Australian Privacy Act."
  intro="We collect as little personal information as we can, use it only to run our business and answer your questions, and never sell it."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {entity} (“All Set”, “we”, “us”) provides Odoo implementation and related consulting services to
    businesses in Australia and Europe. We are responsible for (the “controller” of) the personal
    information collected through this website.
  </p>
  {
    (legal.registration || legal.address) && (
      <p>
        {legal.registration && <>{legal.registration}. </>}
        {legal.address && <>Registered address: {legal.address}.</>}
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    Questions about privacy can go to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy is written to meet the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the
    Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you use our contact form or email us: your name,
      email address and, if you choose to share them, your company, phone number, company size, the
      service you’re interested in and your message.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> When you visit, our hosting provider automatically
      processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, so the
      site can be delivered and kept secure. We don’t use this to identify you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookies and similar technologies.</strong> We only use analytics cookies if you accept
      them. See our <a href={url('/cookies/')}>cookie policy</a> for details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We don’t ask for sensitive information (such as health or financial details) through this
    website, and the site isn’t intended for children.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it, and why</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Replying to your enquiry and arranging a call</td>
        <td>Steps you’ve asked us to take before a possible contract, and our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Running, securing and improving the website</td>
        <td>Our legitimate interest in operating a secure, working website</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Understanding how the website is used (analytics)</td>
        <td>Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Keeping records we’re required to keep</td>
        <td>Legal obligation</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We don’t sell your personal information, we don’t use it for automated decision-making, and we
    only send you news or marketing if you’ve asked us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only with service providers who help us run our business:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>our website host, GitHub (GitHub Pages);</li>
    {formEndpoint && <li>the form service that delivers contact form messages to our inbox;</li>}
    <li>our email and business software providers;</li>
    {analyticsId && <li>Google, for website analytics, only if you accept analytics cookies;</li>}
    <li>professional advisers (such as accountants and lawyers) where needed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may only use the information to provide their services to us. We may also
    disclose information where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We work across Australia and Europe, and some of our providers are based in other countries,
    including the United States. When personal information from the European Economic Area or the
    UK is transferred abroad, we rely on recognised safeguards such as adequacy decisions (including
    the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, where a provider is certified) or the European Commission’s
    Standard Contractual Clauses. For Australian personal information, we take reasonable steps to
    make sure overseas recipients handle it consistently with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry details only for as long as we need them to respond and follow up. If we go on
    to work together, we keep records for the length of the engagement and afterwards for as long
    as the law requires (for example, tax and accounting rules). Otherwise, we delete them once
    they’re no longer needed.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>If you’re in the EU, EEA or UK, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have it corrected if it’s inaccurate, or deleted;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use it;</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent; and</li>
    <li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you’re in Australia, you can ask to access or correct the personal information we hold about
    you. If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your information, please contact us first; you
    can also complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner
    (<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>).
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We’ll reply within one month
    (or 30 days under Australian law), and may need to confirm your identity first.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection, and we take reasonable technical
    and organisational measures to protect personal information from loss, misuse and unauthorised
    access. No system is completely secure, so please avoid sending highly sensitive information
    through the contact form.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our website may link to other sites, such as LinkedIn. Their privacy practices are their own,
    so please read their policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We’ll update this policy when our practices change. The date at the top shows when it was last
    revised.
  </p>
</Legal>
